+  // Adaptive players usually ask for ranges with the Range header, in which
+  // case the URL already names the whole file and there is nothing to do. Some
+  // sites put the range in the query instead, and there the URL names a slice.
+  // Only one such convention is handled, the bytestart/byteend pair, because it
+  // is the only one that has been checked end to end: with those two removed
